    {
      "section": "Cantilever Beam Concept",
      "type": "eval",
      "script": "document.body.style.cssText = 'margin:0; background: #0A0A0F; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; height: 100vh; font-family: Inter, Segoe UI, sans-serif;'; document.body.innerHTML = '<div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:900px\"><div style=\"font-size:36px; font-weight:700; color:#6366f1; margin-bottom:30px\">📐 Cantilever Beam Design</div><div style=\"background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding:40px; border-radius:16px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); text-align:left\"><div style=\"font-size:20px; color:#fff; line-height:2\">A snap-fit clip is a <span style=\"color:#f59e0b; font-weight:700\">flexible cantilever beam</span> with a hook<br><br>1️⃣ Object pushes past the hook<br>2️⃣ Beam deflects (bends slightly)<br>3️⃣ Hook snaps back to retain the object<br><br><div style=\"margin-top:16px; padding:16px; background:rgba(99,102,241,0.15); border-radius:8px; border-left:3px solid #6366f1\"><span style=\"color:#a5b4fc\">Key Parameters:</span><br>Beam length • Beam thickness • Hook height • Entry angle</div></div></div></div>';",
